// t_36492ad8.  A DEFAULT ON A HELPER PARAMETER is legal, and the omitted
// argument is the default EXPRESSION substituted at the call site - not a
// folded constant.  Measured against sce-cgc 475:
//
//     shade(t)  with `float k = 0.5`   is BYTE-IDENTICAL to shade(t, 0.5)
//     `uniform float g; float k = g`   is BYTE-IDENTICAL to shade(t, g),
//                                      and the container carries g as a real
//                                      uniform record
//
// The second is the only shape that separates substitution from folding; every
// literal default passes either way.
//
// REFUSAL: a default may not name ANOTHER PARAMETER of its own function.
// The reference reports C1102 "incompatible type for parameter #3", which
// describes a scope failure as a type error - so this row is pinned by
// VERDICT, never by that text.
float4 shade(float4 c, float k = 0.5, float j = k * 2.0) { return c*k*j; }
float4 main(float4 t : TEXCOORD0) : COLOR { return shade(t); }
